> This PR means that when you are using searchFunction, we will do a shallow clone of the helper at each keystroke (or search). Not a deep clone.

@vvo Got thrown by this as I was trying to use `AlgoliaSearchHelper` and they don't exist. Docs just say `options.searchFunction`'s...["with the helper as a parameter"](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/documentation/#initialization)

At any rate, if I want to call `AlgoliaSearchHelper` methods from within `searchFunction` (e.g. `.on`, `.setPage`), what's the best way to do this?
